		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=5106&amp;p=37015#p37015"><![CDATA[
Your RD-5R center frequency deviation is different than the 878 and 1701. If you have a SDR receiver, you can calibrate it. If you don’t have one you might have to calibrate your hotspot in the middle of all your radios. <br><br>Below is how to calibrate your RD-5R using a SDR receiver. <br>Hope this help,<br>Charlie,<br><br> <strong>iframe</strong> <br><a href="http://youtu.be/8gB0CR20yBc">youtu.be/8gB0CR20yBc</a><p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=5068">KA1CM</a> — Mon May 05, 2025 5:41 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
