		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=5106&amp;p=37005#p37005"><![CDATA[
Hello,<br>I got an RD-5R second hand, installation of OGD77 went fine, thanks to all the devs.<br><br>The issue I have is that the radio cannot 'reach/activate'' the hotspot, error message: Timeout.<br>Two other radios Anytone 878 and DM1701 (OGD77) can activate and communicate through hotspot.<br>RD-5R can communicate via a DMR relais (Hytera RD625), outside the reach from where I'm located.<br><br>What I've checked with the RD-5R:<ul><li>Tried two different MMDVM duplex boards on two different RPis<br>both running latest Pi-Star 4.2.3 with latest HS Hat fw 1.6.1<br>no change with duplex/simplex config</li></ul><ul><li>Both OGD77 releases showing same issue (R20240908 and Beta20250323)</li></ul><ul><li>Frequency deviation seems not the issue, tested with TinySA and SDR</li></ul><ul><li>Calibration seems to be fine (compared with a ham providing screenshots)</li></ul>Any more hints to troubleshoot the issue?<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=8558">DL6EK</a> — Mon May 05, 2025 6:04 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
